// Nationwide HUD FY2026 Fair Market Rent (FMR) baseline — one row per
// zip code, county/metro-area level rents (0BR-4BR), sourced from HUD's
// published FY2026 FMR Schedule
// (huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/fmr2026/FY2026_FMR_Schedule.pdf),
// joined against the Census Bureau's 2020 ZCTA-to-county (and, for the
// six New England states that define FMR areas by town rather than
// county, ZCTA-to-county-subdivision) relationship files
// (www2.census.gov/geo/docs/maps-data/data/rel2020/zcta520/).
//
// This is a NATIONWIDE BASELINE ESTIMATE, not a locally-confirmed
// payment standard — it's the raw county/metro-level FMR HUD publishes,
// not a local housing authority's own payment-standard policy (which is
// usually FMR adjusted by a local PS% and, for Small Area FMR metros,
// published per zip rather than per county). Used only as a fallback
// when no precise `PaymentStandard` row exists for a zip (today: every
// zip outside Duval County, FL — see payment-standards.data.ts for the
// precise, locally-confirmed Jacksonville Housing Authority data) —
// intended to be replaced county-by-county with real local payment
// standards over time, the same way Duval was done first.
//
// 5BR/6BR are not stored here — HUD's nationwide schedule stops at 4BR
// and its own documented rule (FY2026 FMR Schedule, Note 1; 24 CFR
// 888.113) is to add 15% of the 4BR rent per extra bedroom, computed at
// lookup time instead (see properties.service.ts).
export const NATIONWIDE_FMR_BASELINE_EFFECTIVE_DATE = '2025-10-01';

